,"ma-c-cf86c48d40abea30f347","ma-c-d234772b45e8d4a437af","ma-c-dcf022977a54dfa8084f","ma-c-ee88526175b1f4b095e0","ma-c-f1e0d764f630139e572c","ma-c-f5b92dc0cd3434726b95"],"leaves":["ma-c-1438cc02be897900350b","ma-c-14dae89855146e516a05","ma-c-1cbfc929e4525022a1aa","ma-c-386cfa36eab6815b2bb7","ma-c-3ab0af2162f918e5c256","ma-c-458b23d3b5a24041bbe6","ma-c-4bf27c203dedb84e97d3","ma-c-4c58f66589d4654270a5","ma-c-4dd8852a91f7d6182f15","ma-c-6c84349ef5afa30b84a5","ma-c-775ac06eebcaa7c035bc","ma-c-7fff367ac7bc4a118773","ma-c-96aee91f9bc063cc51cb","ma-c-a8f9f329af2c5988e2cd","ma-c-bdf6435612e2abd61daf","ma-c-be6e8d99b6438e9417e0","ma-c-c50a3ba0e165289a4cfa","ma-c-cf86c48d40abea30f347","ma-c-cfd53ce1065fe585754e","ma-c-db6c22bcd61d5813a6cd","ma-c-dcf022977a54dfa8084f","ma-c-ee88526175b1f4b095e0","ma-c-f1e0d764f630139e572c","ma-c-f32daacfb1124ae24d65"],"papers":{"arXiv:1011.0040":{"abstract":"Each square complex matrix is unitarily similar to an upper triangular matrix with diagonal entries in any prescribed order. Let A and B be upper triangular n-by-n matrices that (i) are not similar to direct sums of matrices of smaller sizes, or (ii) are in general position and have the same main diagonal. We prove that A and B are unitarily similar if and only if ||h(A_k)||=||h(B_k)|| for all com","authors":["Douglas Farenick","Vyacheslav Futorny","Tatiana G. Gerasimova"],"year":"2010"},"arXiv:1810.09219":{"abstract":"In representation theory, a classification problem is called wild if it contains the problem of classifying matrix pairs up to simultaneous similarity. The latter problem is considered as hopeless; it contains the problem of classifying an arbitrary finite system of vector spaces and linear mappings between them. We prove that an analogous \"universal\" problem in the theory of tensors of order at m","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Joshua A. Grochow","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2018"},"arXiv:0710.0954":{"abstract":"We give a canonical form for a complex matrix, whose square is normal, under transformations of unitary similarity as well as a canonical form for a real matrix, whose square is normal, under transformations of orthogonal similarity.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Roger A. Horn","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2007"},"arXiv:0710.0810":{"abstract":"Tridiagonal canonical forms of square matrices under congruence or *congruence, pairs of symmetric or skew-symmetric matrices under congruence, and pairs of Hermitian matrices under *congruence are given over an algebraically closed field of characteristic different from 2.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Roger A. Horn","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2007"},"arXiv:0710.0928":{"abstract":"We give canonical matrices of bilinear or sesquilinear forms UxV-->C, (V/U)xV-->C, in which V is a vector space over the field C of complex numbers and U is its subspace.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2007"},"arXiv:1004.3584":{"abstract":"V.I. Arnold [Russian Math. Surveys 26 (2) (1971) 29-43] constructed a miniversal deformation of matrices under similarity; that is, a simple normal form to which not only a given square matrix A but all matrices B close to it can be reduced by similarity transformations that smoothly depend on the entries of B. We construct a miniversal deformation of matrices under congruence.","authors":["Andrii R. Dmytryshyn","Vyacheslav Futorny","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2010"},"arXiv:1105.2160":{"abstract":"V.I. Arnold [Russian Math. Surveys 26(2) (1971) 29-43] constructed a miniversal deformation of a square complex matrix under similarity; that is, a simple normal form to which not only a given square matrix A but all matrices B close to it can be reduced by similarity transformations that smoothly depend on the entries of B. We give miniversal deformations of matrices of sesquilinear forms; that i","authors":["A. Dmytryshyn","V. Futorny","V. V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2011"},"arXiv:1004.3590":{"abstract":"We construct the Hasse diagrams $G_2$ and $G_3$ for the closure ordering on the sets of congruence classes of $2\\times 2$ and $3\\times 3$ complex matrices. In other words, we construct two directed graphs whose vertices are $2\\times 2$ or, respectively, $3\\times 3$ canonical matrices under congruence and there is a directed path from $A$ to $B$ if and only if $A$ can be transformed by an arbitrari","authors":["Andrii Dmytryshyn","Vyacheslav Futorny","Bo Kågström"],"year":"2010"},"arXiv:1304.5762":{"abstract":"We study how small perturbations of a 2-by-2 complex matrix can change its canonical form for *congruence. We construct the Hasse diagram for the closure ordering on the set of *congruence classes of 2-by-2 matrices.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Lena Klimenko","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2013"},"arXiv:1403.2645":{"abstract":"We give a method for constructing a regularizing decomposition of a matrix pencil, which is formulated in terms of the linear mappings. We prove that two pencils are topologically equivalent if and only if their regularizing decompositions coincide up to permutation of summands and their regular parts coincide up to homeomorphisms of their spaces.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Tetiana Rybalkina","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2014"},"arXiv:1704.04670":{"abstract":"W.E. Roth (1952) proved that the matrix equation $AX-XB=C$ has a solution if and only if the matrices $\\left[\\begin{matrix}A&C\\\\0&B\\end{matrix}\\right]$ and $\\left[\\begin{matrix}A&0\\\\0&B\\end{matrix}\\right]$ are similar. A. Dmytryshyn and B. Kågström (2015) extended Roth's criterion to systems of matrix equations $A_iX_{i'}M_i-N_iX_{i''}^{σ_i} B_i=C_i$ $(i=1,\\dots,s)$ with unknown matrices $X_1,\\dot","authors":["Andrii Dmytryshyn","Vyacheslav Futorny","Tetiana Klymchuk"],"year":"2017"},"arXiv:1907.03213":{"abstract":"Our purpose is to give new proofs of several known results about perturbations of matrix pencils. Andrzej Pokrzywa (1986) described the closure of orbit of a Kronecker canonical pencil $A-λB$ in terms of inequalities with pencil invariants. In more detail, Pokrzywa described all Kronecker canonical pencils $K-λL$ such that each neighborhood of $A-λB$ contains a pencil whose Kronecker canonical for","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Tetiana Klymchuk","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2019"}}}